				},
				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "The {{gtClass:TTFactory}} stands ready to create any clients for which it has a valid configuration provided by the vault. This simple scheme works well until you have multiple configurations. Then you have two modes of working, some which return a single client, and some which may return hundreds.\n\nHowever the {{gtClass:TTVault}} of configuration options is organised, all of the options for a client, say \"github_com\", are grouped together. Now the factory can yield a single client, with all of the options selectable form its own private vault; the choice can be made later.\n\nOne github client can flit between repositories, even if they have different authorization requirements. That single client can be cloned into collection of clients, and asynchonously retrieve data, form multiple sites.\n\n\n\n"
			},
